<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<ContentView
    x:Class="LoanCalculatorMaui.Controls.ScenarioExplainerView"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
    xmlns:constants="clr-namespace:LoanCalculator.Core.Constants;assembly=LoanCalculator.Core"
    xmlns:expander="clr-namespace:Syncfusion.Maui.Expander;assembly=Syncfusion.Maui.Expander"
    x:Name="ExplainerRoot">

    <!--
        The plain-language explanation for one What If scenario: what it is for, what every figure
        on the screen above means, what to watch out for, and one line stating what it means for
        this user's own numbers.

        Appended once by ScenarioPage.Configure for whichever scenario is open, so none of the nine
        scenario views know about it. Content comes from ScenarioExplanations.For(scenario) in Core,
        where it is unit-testable.

        COLLAPSED BY DEFAULT. The figures are what people come here for; the explanation is what
        they want the first time and once in a while after that. Expanded by default it would double
        the length of every scenario page.

        ⚠ An SfExpander header does not respond to taps on iOS unless the hosting page calls
        SyncfusionIosTouchFix.ApplyToExpanders — ScenarioPage.OnAppearing does. See CLAUDE.md; this
        defect is silent and cost three failed diagnoses.
    -->
    <Border Style="{DynamicResource ExpanderCardStyle}">
        <expander:SfExpander
            HeaderIconPosition="End"
            IsExpanded="False"
            Style="{DynamicResource CommonExpanderStyle}">

            <expander:SfExpander.Header>
                <Label
                    AutomationId="ScenarioExplainerHeader"
                    Style="{DynamicResource ExpanderHeaderLabelStyle}"
                    Text="{Binding HeaderText, Source={x:Reference ExplainerRoot}}" />
            </expander:SfExpander.Header>

            <expander:SfExpander.Content>
                <VerticalStackLayout Padding="15,4,15,16" Spacing="0">

                    <!--
                        Why this matters.

                        The body's AutomationId lives on this Label rather than on the enclosing
                        layout: a layout is not reliably surfaced as an accessibility element, and a
                        Label with no text measures to zero height and is reported as absent on iOS.
                        Purpose is guaranteed non-empty for all nine scenarios by
                        ScenarioExplanationsTests, which makes this the one anchor a UI test can
                        depend on.
                    -->
                    <Label Style="{DynamicResource PopupFieldLabelStyle}" Text="WHY THIS MATTERS" />
                    <Label
                        Margin="0,4,0,0"
                        AutomationId="ScenarioExplainerBody"
                        FontSize="{DynamicResource LoanAppTextBody}"
                        Text="{Binding Explanation.Purpose, Source={x:Reference ExplainerRoot}}"
                        TextColor="{DynamicResource LoanAppDefaultForegroundColor}" />

                    <!--
                        Worked example, where one exists. Only four of the nine have one, so the
                        whole group collapses rather than leaving an orphan heading — IsVisible is
                        driven from code-behind, because a converter for "is this string empty" is
                        more machinery than one line of C#.
                    -->
                    <VerticalStackLayout x:Name="ExampleSection" Margin="0,14,0,0" Spacing="4">
                        <Label Style="{DynamicResource PopupFieldLabelStyle}" Text="FOR EXAMPLE" />
                        <Label
                            FontAttributes="Italic"
                            FontSize="{DynamicResource LoanAppTextBody}"
                            Opacity="0.85"
                            Text="{Binding Explanation.Example, Source={x:Reference ExplainerRoot}}"
                            TextColor="{DynamicResource LoanAppDefaultForegroundColor}" />
                    </VerticalStackLayout>

                    <!--
                        Reading the numbers — one row per figure on screen above.

                        BindableLayout with a DataTemplate rather than Labels built in code: a
                        code-built Label needs SetDynamicResource for DefaultFontFamily and every
                        theme colour by hand, which is how a control silently stops following the
                        user's font choice. x:DataType makes the two paths compiled bindings, so a
                        typo is a build error rather than an invisible empty Label.
                    -->
                    <Label Margin="0,16,0,0" Style="{DynamicResource PopupFieldLabelStyle}" Text="READING THE NUMBERS" />
                    <VerticalStackLayout
                        Margin="0,6,0,0"
                        Spacing="10"
                        BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding Explanation.ReadingTheNumbers, Source={x:Reference ExplainerRoot}}">
                        <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                            <DataTemplate x:DataType="constants:ExplanationTerm">
                                <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="1">
                                    <Label
                                        FontAttributes="Bold"
                                        FontSize="{DynamicResource LoanAppTextBody}"
                                        Text="{Binding Term}"
                                        TextColor="{DynamicResource LoanAppDefaultForegroundColor}" />
                                    <Label
                                        FontSize="{DynamicResource LoanAppTextBody}"
                                        Opacity="0.75"
                                        Text="{Binding Meaning}"
                                        TextColor="{DynamicResource LoanAppDefaultForegroundColor}" />
                                </VerticalStackLayout>
                            </DataTemplate>
                        </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                    </VerticalStackLayout>

                    <!--  What to watch for  -->
                    <Label Margin="0,16,0,0" Style="{DynamicResource PopupFieldLabelStyle}" Text="WHAT TO WATCH FOR" />
                    <Label
                        Margin="0,4,0,0"
                        FontSize="{DynamicResource LoanAppTextBody}"
                        Opacity="0.85"
                        Text="{Binding Explanation.WatchFor, Source={x:Reference ExplainerRoot}}"
                        TextColor="{DynamicResource LoanAppDefaultForegroundColor}" />

                    <!--
                        The one personalised line, closing the card the same way the data-entry
                        cards close with their own figures. Bound to WhatIfViewModel.
                        PersonalLine, supplied by whoever hosts the card. It used to bind
                        WhatIfViewModel.ScenarioExplainLine directly, which meant the card only
                        worked on a page whose BindingContext was that view model — the reason it
                        could not be reused on the What If Answer tab, which is bound to
                        LoanViewModel.
                    -->
                    <!--
                        Collapses entirely when there is no personalised line. The What If Answer
                        card writes the reader's figures into the explanations themselves, so it
                        has nothing to add here — and a heading over an empty Label just looked
                        like a rendering fault.
                    -->
                    <BoxView x:Name="PersonalLineRule" Style="{DynamicResource FormCardFootRuleStyle}" />
                    <Label x:Name="PersonalLineHeading" Style="{DynamicResource PopupFieldLabelStyle}" Text="IN YOUR CASE" />
                    <!--
                        Not FormCardFootSubStyle: that is FontSizeSmall, right for a figure caption
                        on the entry pages and too small for a sentence here.
                    -->
                    <Label
                        Margin="0,4,0,0"
                        x:Name="PersonalLineLabel"
                        AutomationId="ScenarioExplainerPersonalLine"
                        FontAttributes="Bold"
                        FontSize="{DynamicResource LoanAppTextBody}"
                        Text="{Binding ScenarioExplainLine}"
                        TextColor="{DynamicResource LoanAppDefaultForegroundColor}" />

                </VerticalStackLayout>
            </expander:SfExpander.Content>

        </expander:SfExpander>
    </Border>

</ContentView>
